d as investors bought the dip, fueling a rebound rally on Wall Street.\n4. U.S. stock futures steady after tech-led rebound; CPI in focus\n   Investing.com-- U.S. stock futures were little changed on Monday evening after Wall Street closed sharply higher, with technology shares rebounding from last week's steep selloff, \n5. Nvidia is about 6% of the S&P 500. If Jensen Huang is ousted, there’s no clear successor — could chaos hit portfolios?\n   An Nvidia leadership shake-up could send shockwaves through the market — and analysts are looking ahead to glean how much investor portfolios could be at risk.\n6. Micron, FormFactor, Amkor, Teradyne, and Nvidia shares skyrocket, what you need to know\n   A number of stocks jumped in the morning session after dip-buyers moved into beaten-down semiconductor and hardware names following the sector's steepest one-day rout in 19 months.\n7. Nvidia Faces Class Action Suit Over Huang Allegations; Senator Seeks Probe, Analyst Puts CEO Exit Odds At 15%\n   Fund managers like Cathie Wood and Dan Niles, however, bought the dip in Nvidia shares, and retail traders maintained a bullish view.\n8. Tech leads Asian stock rally as traders track Wall St rebound\n   Asian stocks rallied Tuesday to extend a Wall Street surge led by technology firms as investors took advantage of lower prices following last week's rout, while another plunge in o\n9. Dow Jones Soars 1,132 Points As Amazon, Tesla Rally, But Nvidia Dives; CPI Inflation Report Next\n   Dow Jones futures were in focus after soaring 1,132 points ahead of the CPI inflation report. Amazon and Tesla rallied, but Nvidia dived.\n10. Nvidia CEO admits affair as company launches probe into spy claims\n   Nvidia’s Jensen Huang runs the world’s biggest AI chipmaker company but the woman he’s just admitted to having an extramarital affair with is suspected to have spied for China. CNN\n11. Elon Musk's Cybertruck pivot highlights the founder-CEO advantage\n   With Elon Musk reportedly preparing